P Java Buildpack 2. It supports Apache Tomcat 10, Java 17, and SAP BTP Security Services Integration Libraries 3.x. It also enables usage of Spring Boot 3.x.   To learn more, see:      Documentation: SAP Java Buildpack 2      Blog post: SAP Java Buildpack 2: Jakarta-Based, Fresh and New!    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-23\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3334 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 1.88.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 1 has been updated from version 1.87.0 to 1.88.0. Updated components:      com.sap.xs.onpremise.runtime is updated from version 1.1.7 to 1.1.8      com.sap.hcp.cf.logging is updated from 3.8.1 to 3.8.2      com.sap.cloud.instancemanager is updated from version 2.2.1 to 3.14.0      commons-codec is updated from version 1.16.0 to 1.16.1      otel-agent is updated from version 1.32.0 to 2.0.0      otel-agent-ext-java is updated from version 1.5.8 to 1.5.10    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-23\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3335 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition can now be integrated into SAP Start. This enables access to relevant business content, like cards from the Insights section of the My Home page of SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition as well as searching for and launching apps.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3336 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Resetting snooze or hide actions in the Insights section\nDescription: You can reset all previously applied Snooze or Hide actions, by clicking the Reset Snooze/Hide Actions option below the Insights section. This option enables cards that were snoozed or hidden to be shown again in the Insights section.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-07\nValid as Of: 2024-03-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3337 ---\nComponent: Mobile Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Doc Update: Android push notifications\nDescription: (Version 2402) Google has deprecated the legacy HTTP API that uses Server Key authentication and will discontinue the authentication in June 2024. You must update your configuration to Firebase Service Account Private Key beforehand.  See Configuring Push for Android Apps.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3338 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 5, SAPUI5 version 1.120.9 is used for the administrator", " Apps.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-02-27\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3338 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 5, SAPUI5 version 1.120.9 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2024 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-11\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2402\n\n--- Record 3339 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Referenced SAPUI5 Version\nDescription: As part of hotfix collection 5, SAPUI5 version 1.120.9 is used for the administrator’s SAP Fiori launchpad, SAP-delivered Fiori apps, and the custom-built SAP Fiori apps, which are deployed to the ABAP system.  See SAP BTP ABAP Environment – Maintenance Windows and Major Upgrade Windows in 2024 and SAP UI5\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-11\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3340 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AI API - New Functionalities\nDescription: The following new functionalities are now available when consuming the Data Attribute Recommendation service via AI API:    Support for dataset schemas with overlapping features and labels: Add common values to the list of features and labels in your dataset schemas. Use the trained model for autocomplete tasks.  See Upload Dataset.      Support for masking during model training: Set the training configuration parameter enableMasking to true to make the model learn nontrivial relationships between inputs and outputs (even when the list of features coincides with the list of labels).  See Training Configuration.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-03-06\nValid as Of: 2024-03-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 831 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Table Columns for Number of Notes\nDescription: In the Tasks table of a task list, you can now find two new columns that provide information about the number of notes a task has. One column provides the number of notes added during the planning stage of a task list, meaning that these notes have been uploaded in the Manage Closing Task Lists app. The second column provides the number of notes added during the processing of a task, meaning that those notes have been uploaded in the Process Closing Tasks app.  App affected:  Process Closing Tasks\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 832 ---\nComponent: SAP Health Data Services for FHIR\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Signature Verification for FHIR packages\nDescription: When a FHIR package is published, a checksum hash is generated and sent to the server along with the package for integrity verification  Additionally, SAP Health Data Services for FHIR CLI verifies the integrity of the downloaded FHIR packages using the checksum hash provided along with the package.  Refer to Publish a FHIR Package Using the CLI and Download a FHIR Package Using the CLI for more information. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 833 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Upcoming Outbound IP Addresses Changes in Azure Data Centers Require Customer Action\nDescription: The outbound IP addresses of SAP Data Intelligence Cloud in Azure data centers are planned to change in a near future release. The access from SAP Data Intelligence to your external data sources that are protected by a network access tool such as a firewall will fail if the new outbound IP addresses are not maintained. As part of the SAP Data Intelligence 2025.08 release, both the current and preserved outbound IP addresses will be available in the INFO_NAT_GATEWAY_IP connection information within the Connection Management application. Please add the preserved outbound IP addresses for SAP Data Intelligence Cloud to the allow-list of your external data sources. SAP recommends completing this action by August 1, 2025 as the outbound IP addresses will be switched afterward.  For more information, see SAP Note 3588293 .\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-05-17\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 834 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ABAP SQL Consumption Model\nDescription: You can now use the ABAP SQL Consumption Model Generator to generate corresponding CDS external entities for each entity that is exposed in a SQL service. Furthermore, you can use it for each entity that has no SQL service in the imported CSN(s) of the remote system. This also includes the generation of any potential simple types that the entity may contain.  See ABAP SQL Consumption Model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 835 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ADT Links in IDE Action HTML Results\nDescription: ADT Links can now be incorporated in the HTML result of an IDE action, allowing users to navigate to development objects in ABAP development tools for Eclipse.  See Implementing a \"Focused Objects Display Action with an HTML Result and Working with IDE Actions .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 836 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating and Editing CDS Table Entities\nDescription: You can now create and edit CDS table entities (in short, table entities) in the source-based editor of data definitions.  See Creating a Data Definition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 837 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating and Editing Electronic Document Consistency Scenarios\nDescription: Customers and partners can now create consistency scenarios in their ABAP projects. This feature lets them check the consistency of their business documents across systems. To set up these scenarios, users create and configure representation types, comparison types, checks, events, and inconsistency categories.  See Working with Electronic Document Consistency Scenarios.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 838 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Launchpad App Descriptor Items\nDescription: Customers and partners can now create and maintain launchpad app descriptor", "\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 838 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating Launchpad App Descriptor Items\nDescription: Customers and partners can now create and maintain launchpad app descriptor items in ABAP development tools for Eclipse. A launchpad app descriptor item describes how an application is started and is required to bring newly developed apps into the SAP Fiori launchpad.   See Creating Launchpad App Descriptor Items.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 839 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Creating SAP Fiori App Using Quick Fiori Application Generator\nDescription: You can now create a List Report-based Fiori application from service binding using the Quick Fiori Application generator.  See Creating SAP Fiori App Using Quick Fiori Application Generator.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n--- Record 840 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: Improvements in the ABAP Coverage View\nDescription: You can now use the following new features within the ABAP Coverage view:  Changing the coverage scope: You can modify the coverage scope of development objects or packages to evaluate their coverage numbers in detail.  Exclude from coverage: By excluding selected objects from your coverage result, you can change the aggregated coverage measurement result.    See Evaluating ABAP Unit Code Coverage Results and ABAP Coverage View.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: nan\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-16\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2505\n\n", "--- Record 1791 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Diagnostics Task\nDescription: You can now create a new garbage collection logging task in Diagnostics. See: Diagnostics\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1792 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Filter in Diagnostics\nDescription: You can now filter the diagnostic tasks list to locate specific tasks.   See: Diagnostics\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1793 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Edge Integration Cell: 8.23.*    Increment: 2410  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1794 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Functions in Mapping Guidelines\nDescription: Functions in Mapping Guideline editor now supports XSLT 3.0 and XPath 3.1.  See: Functions\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1795 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:   SAP Integration Advisor: 1.93.*    Increment: 2410    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1796 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: xCBL Type System\nDescription: The Type System library now includes the new xCBL type system. The content of the system will be rolled-out in a phased manner post-release.  See: Overview Of B2B Standards\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1797 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Manage requests via APIs\nDescription: You can now create and delete business solution and interface requests using the newly added APIs. You are also able to use the APIs to submit, complete, and reopen business solution requests.  For further details, see API Reference on SAP Business Accelerator Hub and Integration Assessment APIs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1798 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.34.*      Increment: 2410    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1799 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Evaluation of Extended Receiver Determinations\nDescription: Rules have been added for analyzing operation mappings in extended receiver determinations. The additional information is reported in the full evaluation result spreadsheet.  Please note that to view this new information, you will need to perform a new data extraction. For more details on how to extract the your data, visit Create a Data Extraction Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n--- Record 1800 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.34.*      Increment: 2410    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-07\nValid as Of: 2024-12-07\nVersion: 2410\n\n", "--- Record 1331 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Troubleshooting entity deletion\nDescription: Documentation for troubleshooting the most frequent reasons for deletion of entities from a target system by the Identity Provisioning is now available. For more information, see Entity Deletion Issues.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1332 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.11.1\nDescription: This version brings the following changes:  We've introduced Istio-based local rate limiting, which you can configure using the new RateLimit custom resource. For more information, see RateLimit Custom Resource and Local Rate Limiting Configuration.  We've fixed the issue where a workload exposed via a v2alpha1 APIRule was not accessible from within the cluster.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1333 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.11.2\nDescription: We have reverted the previously released fix for issue #1632 because it added an additional AuthorizationPolicy with action ALLOW, which was difficult to override.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-18\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1334 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription:   We've added Undo and Redo buttons to the global toolbar. These buttons enable you to reverse up to 100 previous changes in the app. Each undo or redo action is shown in its respective canvas.    We have decommissioned the system variables systemVars.releaseEnv and systemVars.env, as they're no longer in use.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1335 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Reserved Until for Reservation and Extend Reservation Requests in Coupon Management Service\nDescription: You now have the Reserved Until parameter available for reservation and extend reservation requests in the Coupon Management service.   It indicates the time till which the coupon is reserved in a transaction.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1336 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Improved Onboarding for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition with all-tasks Service Plan\nDescription: If you are setting up SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition with the all-tasks service plan, you don't need to create an additional ticket to enable the destination anymore. This step is now automated. For more information, see Connect SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition and SAP Task Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-25\nValid as Of: 2025-02-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1337 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Belize theme disabled as base for new themes.\nDescription: The Belize theme is disabled as a base for creating new themes. If you are using a theme based on Belize, please note that the Belize theme has been deprecated for theming since August 28, 2024. UI frameworks like SAPUI5 and Unified Rendering no longer support Belize themes in their latest versions. It is recommended to migrate your theme to a Horizon or Quartz theme. You can find a how-to guide at Migrating Themes.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1338 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Change Log Duration Parameter for Repository Onboarding and Updates\nDescription: We have introduced the changeLogDuration parameter as an optional setting in Document Management Service, Integration Option, allowing you to choose how much historical change log data they retrieve, which helps you to reduce errors related to outdated tokens and improves usability by setting the maximum duration to 2160 hours.  See Internal Repository.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-24\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1339 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Owner Visibility in Key Properties\nDescription: The Document Management Service, Application Option now displays the owner of the document under the Key Properties tab instead of labeling them as Administrator in the Access Control tab. This update helps you add or update the owner’s name as an Access Control List (ACL), which then propagates to subfolders and documents.   Previously, the owner appeared as an ACL principal in the application", " Record 1339 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Owner Visibility in Key Properties\nDescription: The Document Management Service, Application Option now displays the owner of the document under the Key Properties tab instead of labeling them as Administrator in the Access Control tab. This update helps you add or update the owner’s name as an Access Control List (ACL), which then propagates to subfolders and documents.   Previously, the owner appeared as an ACL principal in the application UI, which confused users regarding the difference between the owner and the ACL. By relocating the owner details to the Key Properties tab, we enhance clarity around the object owner and the associated ACLs, thereby improving the overall user experience. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-24\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1340 ---\nComponent: Document Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Thumbnail Generation Enhancement for Document Updates\nDescription: Thumbnail generation has been enhanced to support document update scenarios, allowing for the automatic creation of a thumbnail whenever a document is updated with a new version, thereby providing you with a visual representation of the latest content, which was previously unsupported.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-24\nValid as Of: 2025-02-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1191 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 48.1.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 48.0.0 to 48.1.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.1.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1192 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Mobile\nDescription: We've improved governance and security by removing the option to upload the iOS distribution certificate when creating iOS build configurations. You can now build your iOS project using your Team ID and then perform code-signing on your macOS device. For more information, see iOS Builds\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1193 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Apps\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Web & Mobile\nDescription:   You can now generate app pages using AI. The Generate Pages feature is designed to streamline the application development process by enabling you to automatically create pages based on the data entities already integrated in your project. For more information, see Generate Pages Using AI      We've introduced a new context menu that you can access by right-clicking on a component in the UI canvas or the layout tree. The menu allows you to perform common actions like cut, copy, paste, duplicate and delete. Additionally, you can also select the parent UI element, wrap the selected element in a new container, or show and hide the Logic canvas.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1194 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Identity Authentication is the Default Authentication Mechanism for New Subscriptions\nDescription: For new subscriptions to SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition and SAP SuccessFactors Work Zone, the default authentication method is now Identity Authentication. Existing subscriptions will not be affected.  Make sure that you have an OIDC-based trust between SAP Cloud Identity Services – Identity Authentication and SAP BTP. For more information, see Establish Trust and Federation Between SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service and SAP Cloud Identity Services\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-13\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502B\n\n--- Record 1195 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: User Profile Information From SCIM API\nDescription: If the setting Use profile information from the SCIM API is enabled in the Features screen, more attributes are now taken from the SCIM API: location, nickname, and display name. These attributes can be viewed in the user profile and are read-only.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502B\n\n--- Record 1196 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Wizard Enhancements\nDescription: The wizard has been enhanced as follows:   Easier access to wizard creation. When you create a new section, you can now choose between a Wizard section type or a Freestyle section type.  A new setting defines whether the wizard is collapsible and what is the default mode – expanded or collapsed.   If a wizard can be executed multiple times, you can now define if the multiple executions can run in parallel (before completing the previous runs).  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-20\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502B\n\n--- Record 1197 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Identity Authentication is the Default Authentication Mechanism for New Subscriptions\nDescription: For new subscriptions to SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition, the default authentication method is now Identity Authentication. Existing subscriptions will not be affected.  Make sure that you have an OIDC-based trust between SAP Cloud Identity Services – Identity Authentication and SAP BTP. For more information, see Establish Trust and Federation Between SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service and SAP Cloud Identity Services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-13\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: 2502B\n\n--- Record 1198 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.26.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.25.0 to 2.26.0. Updated components:      Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.35 to 10.1.36      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.23.8 to 2.23.9      The SLF", " Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.26.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.25.0 to 2.26.0. Updated components:      Tomcat 10 is updated from version 10.1.35 to 10.1.36      SAP HANA Driver (hana.driver.2.X.X) is updated from version 2.23.8 to 2.23.9      The SLF4J component (org.slf4j) is updated from version 2.0.16 to 2.0.17      SnakeYAML is updated from version 2.2 to 2.3      org.apache.httpcomponents.core5.httpcore5 is updated from version 5.3.1 to 5.3.3      logback is updated from version 1.5.16 to 1.5.17      com.sap.xs.onpremise.runtime is updated from version 1.3.3 to 1.3.4    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-06\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1199 ---\nComponent: SAP Start\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Identity Authentication is the Default Authentication Mechanism for New Subscriptions\nDescription: For new subscriptions to SAP Start, the default authentication method is now Identity Authentication. Existing subscriptions will not be affected.  Make sure that you have an OIDC-based trust between SAP Cloud Identity Services – Identity Authentication and SAP BTP. For more information, see Establish Trust and Federation Between SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service and SAP Cloud Identity Services.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-13\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1200 ---\nComponent: SAPUI5\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: SAPUI5 Distribution 1.134\nDescription: SAPUI5 version 1.134 has been released for UI development and can now be consumed by SAP BTP services. It’s up to the services to determine when they start using the new version.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-19\nValid as Of: 2025-03-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_f9d82a87d8e4c8510a8a3f0bc245686cd7411349341964af06ed68eb01856325_v2"}